{%- doc -%}
  Renders the <img> element using provided image object

  Deferred by default. Nothing here used to say when to fetch, so every caller
  inherited the HTML default — eager — and a collection page pulled all thirty of
  its cards at once, the twenty-odd below the fold included. `lazy` is the right
  answer for almost everything this renders, so it is the default and the few
  images that are on screen at first paint say so.

  **Pass `height`.** Left out, the source is the image's own height — a 1720px
  original for a 215px box — and the 2x and 3x entries ask for more than the file
  has, so all three collapse onto the same original. It is not a fallback anyone
  wants; it is what happens when the argument is forgotten.

  For an image whose box is a share of the viewport rather than a fixed height,
  this snippet is the wrong tool: a 1x/2x/3x srcset describes one rendered size,
  and a card in a responsive grid has several. Those emit `image_tag` with `widths`
  and `sizes` themselves — see [ui-product-card] and [ui-product-gallery].

  @param {object} image - image object
  @param {number} [height] - the height the image is drawn at, in CSS pixels
  @param {string} [class] - additional classes
  @param {string} [loading] - `lazy` (the default) or `eager`. Eager for anything
    above the fold: a lazy hero is slower than no attribute at all, because the
    browser stops treating it as urgent.
  @param {string} [text_fallback] - text to display if image is blank
  @param {boolean} [unset_image_tag] - if true, ignores the image focal point
  @param {string} [style] - additional styles

  @example
  {% render 'image', image: product.featured_image, height: 300, class: 'product-image' %}
{%- enddoc -%}
{% if image != blank %}
  {% assign image_height = height | default: image.height %}
  {% assign image_height_2x = height | default: image_height | times: 2 %}
  {% assign image_height_3x = height | default: image_height | times: 3 %}
  {% assign image_loading = loading | default: 'lazy' %}

  {% capture image_srcset -%}
    {{ image | image_url: height: image_height }} 1x, {{ image | image_url: height: image_height_2x }} 2x, {{ image | image_url: height: image_height_3x }} 3x
  {%- endcapture %}

  {% assign style_value = style | default: '' %}

  {% if unset_image_tag %}
    {% assign style_value = style_value | append: 'object-position: inherit;' %}
  {% endif %}

  {{
    image
    | image_url: height: image_height
    | image_tag: class: class, srcset: image_srcset, style: style_value, loading: image_loading
  }}
{% elsif text_fallback %}
  {{ text_fallback }}
{% endif %}
